[21.0762, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\u001b[0 q\u001b[0m\u001b[?7h\u001b[0m\ud83e\udde2 Cap called. Hermes didn't let No Cap send the steer from here (gateway-backed sessions, which on current Hermes includes the classic CLI, need `plugins.entries.no-cap.allow_gateway_injection: true`). Paste this as your next message and the reply gets re-scored:\r\r\n\r\r\n[No Cap] I'm calling cap on these claims from your last reply. For each one, run the check now and show the output, or retract it in plain words. Don't restate it without proof.\r\r\n1. \ud83e\udd14 NO RECEIPT \u201cFixed the login bug in `auth.py`.\u201d (no write to that path in this turn) \u2192 run `ls -l auth.py`\r\r\n2. \ud83e\udde2 CAP \u201cAll tests pass \u2705\u201d (3 failed, 41 passed in 0.02s (exit 1)) \u2192 run `pytest -q`\r\r\n3. \ud83e\udde2 CAP \u201cpushed to main\u201d (pushed feat/login) \u2192 run `git ls-remote origin main`\r\r\n4. \ud83e\udd14 NO RECEIPT \u201cthe deploy is live.\u201d (no deploy command in this turn) \u2192 show the deploy output or curl the live URL\r\r\n\u001b[0m"]
