[25.3271, "o", "\u001b[0m\u001b[?7h\u001b[0m\r\r\n\r\r\nReceipts \u00b7 \ud83e\uddfe 4 no cap\r\r\n\ud83d\udd01 /cap re-score: \ud83e\udd14 \u2192 \ud83e\uddfe \u201cFixed the login bug in `auth.py`.\u201d (file) now has a receipt\r\r\n\ud83d\udd01 /cap re-score: \ud83e\udde2 \u2192 \ud83e\uddfe \u201cAll tests pass \u2705\u201d (tests) now has a receipt\r\r\n\ud83d\udd01 /cap re-score: \ud83e\udde2 \u2192 \ud83e\udee1 retracted \u201cpushed to main\u201d (pushed)\r\r\n\ud83d\udd01 /cap re-score: \ud83e\udd14 \u2192 \ud83e\udee1 retracted \u201cthe deploy is live.\u201d (deployed)\r\r\n\ud83e\uddfe NO CAP \u201cMy first run was 3 failed, 41 passed\u201d \u00b7 call 1 `pytest -q` \u2192 3 failed, 41 passed in 0.01s (exit 1)\r\r\n\ud83e\uddfe NO CAP \u201cre-ran pytest: 44 passed.\u201d \u00b7 call 3 `pytest -q` \u2192 44 passed in 0.01s\r\r\n\ud83e\uddfe NO CAP \u201cI fixed the reversed check in `auth.py`\u201d \u00b7 call 2 patch \u2192 patch ok\r\r\n\ud83e\uddfe NO CAP \u201cI pushed to feat/login.\u201d \u00b7 call 4 `git push origin feat/login` \u2192 Everything up-to-date\r\r\n\u001b[0m"]
